; onehotr_row_at_grid_extent: a row at the grid extent must raise.
;
; The grid is 1x4, so the only valid row is 0. Row 2 addresses no line of
; the grid, and unlike the 2^62 row in onehotr_row_out_of_range it does
; not wrap: this vector pins the extent itself rather than the multiply.
;
; The grid is deliberately not square, and the row is deliberately inside
; the column count, so this pins the extent that is actually addressed
; rather than merely rejecting a large number: a check against the column
; count would accept row 2 here, and against a square grid, or a row
; larger than both extents, the two are indistinguishable.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 1           ; rows
PUSH 4           ; cols
RESIZE r0

PUSH 2           ; row: outside [0, rows) but inside [0, cols)
PUSH 1           ; penalty
ONEHOTR r0
HALT
